 "text": "Hey! How's everything going? Running shoes, a warm sweatshirt, and a comfy cap for cold runs. A water bottle and a snack for after race are nice too. Running in the morning before work can be nice, but it' cold. Running after work is better weather but you're rushed. A simple stopwatch is great start. There are running apps that track your distance and pace too, but a simple timer works for now. Headlamps are handy for dark runs. Soaks are worth it in winter. You can keep one in your bag at work and swap out on cold morning.",
